    {
      "id": "I49Sg",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{NiSO}_{4} \\cdot 6 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{array}{lllll}\\text { Ion } & \\mathrm{Mn}^{2+} & \\mathrm{Cu}^{2+} & \\mathrm{Fe}^{2+} & \\mathrm{Ni}^{2+} \\\\ \\text { EC } & 3 d^{5} & 3 d^{9} & 3 d^{6} & 3 d^{8} \\\\ \\text { Number of } & 5 & 1 & 4 & 2\\end{array}$ \r\nunpaired electron \r\nHence lowest paramagnetism is shown by $\\mathrm{CuSO}_{4} \\cdot 5 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$",
